ragnaros for Debian
===================

First use
---------

The modprobe option in /usr/lib/modprobe.d/ragnaros-usbhid.conf keeps usbhid
off the deck so the daemon can claim it with libusb. usbhid usually loads from
the initramfs, which the package refreshes through the update-initramfs
trigger, so reboot once after the first install. Then, as the user who sits at
the deck:

    systemctl --user enable --now ragnarosd

The daemon is not enabled for anyone by default: only users with the deck
plugged in want it. ragnaros-gif-refresh.timer, which downloads GIF themes
from Tenor, is opt-in the same way.

Missing key icons
-----------------

The Debian package does not ship the key icons upstream renders from
third-party application logos (Chrome, Discord, WhatsApp, VS Code and others;
see debian/copyright). The bundled profiles still load, and the keys that name
one of those icons stay blank. To fill them, put a PNG with the same relative
path under ~/.local/share/ragnaros/ or ~/.config/ragnaros/assets/, for example:

    ~/.local/share/ragnaros/icons/firefox.png

ragnaros paths lists every directory the daemon reads.

 -- Valentin Torassa <valentintorassacolombero@gmail.com>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 14:42:59 -0300
